session Temporal_Planning_Base = Temporal_Munta_Base +
  description \<open>Thin layer loading the Analysis-free Formal-PDDL-Semantics discrete semantics
    (Discrete_Planning_Common / Discrete_Temporal_Planning: the temporal happening and
    state-sequence semantics and well-formedness) and the grounder's temporal normalization locales
    (session Grounding_Temporal_Common: grounded_temporal_problem / positive_temporal_problem) on top
    of the stable Munta heap. The FPS sessions are checked HERE, ABOVE the Munta heap, so editing
    them rebuilds only this layer and the ones above; every FPS theory the sessions above import is
    loaded into this heap so they never re-check it. The Analysis-tainted FPS checkers
    (Temporal_PDDL_Checker_*, the continuous reduction) are dropped entirely -- the net builder uses
    an in-repo Analysis-free wf-checker. The whole development is built on top of this heap in
    jEdit. Contains no project-local theories (FPS + grounder externals only).\<close>
  options [timeout = 7200]
  sessions
    "Utils"
    "Discrete_Planning_Common"
    "Discrete_Temporal_Planning"
    "Grounding_Temporal_Common"
  theories [document = false]
    "Discrete_Planning_Common.Utils"
    "Discrete_Planning_Common.Happening_Semantics"
    "Discrete_Temporal_Planning.Temporal_Instantiations"
    "Discrete_Temporal_Planning.Temporal_Utils"
    "Discrete_Temporal_Planning.Temporal_Happening_Semantics"
    "Discrete_Temporal_Planning.Temporal_State_Sequence_Semantics"
    "Grounding_Temporal_Common.Temporal_PDDL_Normalization"
